Body:
Hi all,
I just had access to augment and wanted to make it a bit more open. So I created an OpenAI-Compatible proxy for their SDK (Thanks to Qwen3.6 and Claude).
The beautiful thing is that I was able to make (almost) all features work: model list fetching from CLI, chat messages direct and streamed, reasoning content, tool calling AND image input, there was a need to patch the payload for this one as their SDK just drops image nodes from the prompt, so I'm labeling this as experimental and could break at any update.
What's still missing unfortunately is reasoning_effort, as it seems from the CLI that opus does support it, though I wasn't able to find a way to get it to work through the SDK so far.

So I tested the proxy a bit in OpenWebUI and OpenCode and it's doing great so far. But be warned, this is vibe-coded in 2 days, it has a healthy amount of tests, including end-to-end using the real API and your auth token, so I think it should be fine. Review the code if you want and send me feedback. I'm not a webdev mainly (my specialty is Cpp/Python/Unreal Engine)

https://github.com/charnet3d/augment-openai-proxy



